# The lantern, at home on the little table by your bunk. Cheerful, and
# cheerfully wrong about where home is; underneath, a little tender.
# Placeholder writing: rewrite freely.
#
# The news_* flags are set by the game when something happens that he wasn't
# there to see (a fish caught). He
# asks about the first one waiting, then forgets it.

~ start
? lantern_low
-> low
? deck_talk and not at_cove
-> bedtime
? news_fish
-> fish
? morning
lantern: Morning! Did you sleep? I don't. I just glow quieter.
? else
lantern: There you are. I kept your place warm. Well. Warm-ish.
-> ask

~ fish
clear news_fish
lantern: You smell of fish. Was it a good fish?
- A fine one. -> fish_fine
- It looked like it knew the way. -> fish_knew

~ fish_fine
lantern: A fine fish! Is home a fish? ...No. Probably not.
-> ask

~ fish_knew
lantern: They always do. They never say.
-> ask

~ ask
- Where's home, do you think? -> home
? not asked_follow
- Why don't you come with me? -> follow
? met_heron
- Is the captain always like that? -> captain
- Just saying hello. -> bye

~ home
? talked.lantern >= 3
lantern: The next island. *Definitely* the next one.
? else
lantern: Close. I know exactly where it is. Roughly.
-> ask

~ follow
set asked_follow
lantern: I'd like to. But somebody has to keep your bunk warm.
lantern: And you always come back here. So this is where I'll be.
-> ask

~ captain
lantern: Always. He likes you, though. He said "hm" in the nice way.
-> ask

~ bye
lantern: Hello! And goodbye. And hello again, later.
-> END

# Home from the sea, low (#158): he gave you nearly all his light (#183)
# and he's barely lit, but he talks (#184). He won't give the old book's
# clue away: only once you've read it does he think of spicy food. Fed the
# remedy, he's himself again (#155).
~ low
lantern: Oh, hello again!
? read_fire_spirits
-> spicy
lantern: I'm feeling a little better. I think.
@look lantern tired
lantern: Well, perhaps not.
-> END

~ spicy
lantern: Spicy food?
lantern: I do like spicy food.
lantern: I don't think I've ever had any, though.
-> END

# After the deck talk (#187): bed, and the island by morning.
~ bedtime
lantern: Off to your bunk! We'll be there by morning.
lantern: I'll keep a lookout. I'm very good at looking out.
-> END
